# CI except-pass allowlist
#
# Each non-comment line below is a path RELATIVE TO REPO ROOT that is
# permitted to contain a bare `except: pass` pattern. The path MUST be
# followed (on the same physical line) by a `# reason:` comment explaining
# why the swallow is safe.
#
# The intent of the CI guard (see scripts/check_except_pass.sh and NFM-2219)
# is to keep this file EMPTY. Every line here is technical debt that must
# be re-justified at every PR that touches it. Add an entry only when the
# exception is genuinely defensible and the cost of logging outweighs the
# observability benefit — in nearly every case, replacing `pass` with
# `logger.debug(...)` is the right move.
#
# Format:
#   <relative/path/to/file.py>  # reason: <one-line justification>
#
# Example:
#   apps/api/src/nfm_db/legacy/foo.py  # reason: third-party shim, error is irrelevant
